    "CommitMsg": "Post merge fixes for #3720\n\n1. Null fields on edit: initializeForm now turns null into '' for every\n   text field, so the edit page no longer crashes on addresses without a\n   zip code or street.\n2. Length errors: zip code and street address now show a mat-error\n   (MAX_TEXTAREA_LENGTH) when they are too long.\n3. Double submit: the Submit button is also disabled while saving\n   (addressForm().submitting()).\n4. Failed save: the catch in save() no longer calls resetForm(), so the\n   user's input survives a server error. I rewrote the two existing\n   tests that expected the form to be cleared; they now check that the\n   values are kept.\n5. Mobile number range: the minimum is now 1000000, matching the server\n   and the error text. The range in the error message is built from the\n   same constants.\n6. Address list reload: AddressComponent.load() now goes through a\n   Subject with switchMap, catchError and takeUntilDestroyed, like the\n   review fix in f1312b0. load() is still public, so RecycleComponent\n   keeps working.\n7. Edit route: paramMap now uses switchMap into getById with\n   takeUntilDestroyed, so a late response for an old id can't overwrite\n   the form. A failed getById is now logged.\n8. Dead code: removed addressId and getMessage from\n   AddressSelectComponent, plus their spec case.\n9. Duplicated SCSS: the page sizing moved into address.component.scss as\n   :host(.page-card). Both pages already set that class, but nothing\n   used it before. The two page stylesheets now contain only\n   .center-container. I left that class duplicated, because almost every\n   page component in the repo has its own copy and moving it would go\n   beyond this change.\n10. Shared schema: new file\n    frontend/src/app/Models/address-form.schema.ts holds\n    AddressFormModel, addressFormSchema and the limit constants. The\n    template now uses those constants instead of hard-coded 8, 160 and\n    the range string.\n\nSigned-off-by: Jannik Hollenbach \u003cjannik.hollenbach@owasp.org\u003e",
    "Author": "Jannik Hollenbach \u003cjannik.hollenbach@owasp.org\u003e",
    "Committer": "Jannik Hollenbach \u003cjannik.hollenbach@owasp.org\u003e"
  },
